akePHP Version: 3.5.11.\r\n* Platform and Target: ubuntu 16.04 LTS, runtime docker php 7.0-fpm, nginx.\r\n\r\n### What you did\r\nRender a date control with required attribute set on true.\r\n```php\r\n<?= $this->Form->control('date', ['type' => 'date', 'required' => true]) ?>\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n### What happened\r\nIt render the container div with the `required` class but the selects doesn't have the required attribute.\r\n```html\r\n<div class=\"input date required\">\r\n    <label>Date</label>\r\n    <select name=\"date[year]\">...</select>\r\n    <select name=\"date[month]\">...</select>\r\n    <select name=\"date[day]\">...</select>\r\n</div>\r\n```\r\n\r\n### What you expected to happen\r\nIt should add the required attribute to each select\r\n```html\r\n<div class=\"input date required\">\r\n    <label>Date</label>\r\n    <select name=\"date[year]\" required=\"required\">...</select>\r\n    <select name=\"date[month]\" required=\"required\">...</select>\r\n    <select name=\"date[day]\" required=\"required\">...</select>\r\n</div>\r\n```\r\n\r\nI was deepening into the framework code and this small patch works for me. I was the first solutions that came out after reading the code a bit, but I didn't run any tests.\r\n\r\n```php\r\n<?php\r\n    // insert after this line\r\n    // https://github.com/cakephp/cakephp/blob/b557240fc11cdce9e60d35d4a911c01c0f28b5ee/src/View/Helper/FormHelper.php#L2436\r\n    // \r\n    if (isset($options['required']) && is_array($options[$type])) {\r\n        $options[$type]['required'] = (bool)$options['required'];\r\n    }\r\n?>\r\n```\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"markstory","id":24086,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MDg2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24086?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory","html_url":"https://github.com/markstory","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/following{/other_user}","gists_